files/reactions-cdxml.csv is Chem's demo table of reaction schemes as CDXML (the owner's note on decision 16, 2026-11-14).
Its "cdxml" column holds eight files copied from three projects' test data, unchanged but for the two changes noted
under RDKit and Ketcher, fetched 2026-11-09 from each repository's default branch; "written by" is each file's
CreationProgram, "source" its repository path and licence.

RDKit
  rxn1.cdxml, reaction-with-boc.cdxml, chemdraw_template8.cdxml, chemdraw_template6.cdxml
  from https://github.com/rdkit/rdkit, Code/GraphMol/test_data/CDXML/, licensed under RDKit's BSD 3-Clause License,
  reproduced at the end of this notice.
  Changed here, 2026-11-15: rxn1.cdxml's phenylboronic acid restored: an extra carbon removed (its fragment drew
  Ph-BH-C(OH)2: the carbon between the boron and the two OH dropped, the OH bonded to the boron at the page's bond
  length, the boron's H and its "BH" label made "B").

Indigo (EPAM Systems)
  Suzuki_Rxn1.cdxml, N-Sulfonylation_Rxn1.cdxml (api/tests/integration/tests/formats/cdxml/) and
  reactions_with_brackets_2801.cdxml (api/tests/integration/tests/rendering/reactions/)
  from https://github.com/epam/Indigo, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Ketcher
Copyright (C) 2018 EPAM Systems
This product includes software developed at EPAM Systems, Inc.
  schema-with-two-retrosynthetic-arrows.cdxml (ketcher-autotests/tests/test-data/CDXML/)
  from https://github.com/epam/ketcher, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
  Changed here, 2026-11-15: its six methyl carbons restored from Ketcher's Mn labels (each node written as
  Element="25" NumHydrogens="0" with the text "Mn" is a plain carbon again, its id and position kept; the scheme is
  acetylacetone and thiourea to 4,6-dimethylpyrimidine-2-thione).

